# HELP js_callback_deliveries_total Tries of jobs' completion callbacks whose answer was recorded, by result: delivered (a 2xx), abandoned (a 410), failed (any other status, a timeout, a refused connection, a redirect or a name that did not resolve) or refused-address (the address rule refused an address of the receiver, and nothing was sent).
# TYPE js_callback_deliveries_total counter
js_callback_deliveries_total{result="delivered"} 1
js_callback_deliveries_total{result="abandoned"} 2
js_callback_deliveries_total{result="failed"} 3
js_callback_deliveries_total{result="refused-address"} 4
# HELP js_placement_refusals_total Refusals of a host to a queued job by the placement, by host and by the predicate that refused: cpu (CPU slack), cpu-curve (the curve hosts' slot-by-slot CPU check), predicted-memory (the load predicate's memory side), booked-memory (the flat memory guard) or cold-cap. A job is counted once for each host that refused it, in each pass.
# TYPE js_placement_refusals_total counter
js_placement_refusals_total{host="host-a",reason="cpu"} 3
js_placement_refusals_total{host="host-a",reason="predicted-memory"} 1
js_placement_refusals_total{host="host-b",reason="booked-memory"} 2
# HELP js_curve_wait_expiries_total Queued jobs of a curve class that waited past the wait bound (server.curve_max_wait_seconds) with no host fitting their curve, and were tested with their flat number from then on. A rise means curves book more than the hosts can give.
# TYPE js_curve_wait_expiries_total counter
js_curve_wait_expiries_total 2
# HELP js_agent_start_refusals_total Job starts a host's agent refused, by host and refusal code (the agent's code, or other), counted when the refusal is recorded, whether the job then goes back to the queue or fails.
# TYPE js_agent_start_refusals_total counter
js_agent_start_refusals_total{host="host-a",code="no-capacity"} 2
js_agent_start_refusals_total{host="host-b",code="input-not-allowed"} 1
# HELP js_agent_bodies_too_large_total Agents' hellos and heartbeats refused 413 body-too-large, their body over the cap the server reads (65536 bytes), by route. The agent ends at such an answer, so each is an agent that stopped.
# TYPE js_agent_bodies_too_large_total counter
js_agent_bodies_too_large_total{route="hello"} 1
js_agent_bodies_too_large_total{route="heartbeat"} 2
# HELP js_unknown_jobs_found_total Jobs a host's heartbeat listed that the store holds no record of, by host, each counted once, at the beat that first listed it. They are kept running as orphans of the host, which takes no job while it lists one.
# TYPE js_unknown_jobs_found_total counter
js_unknown_jobs_found_total{host="host-a"} 5
# HELP js_unknown_listing_guarded_total Heartbeats whose listing was more than half jobs the store holds no record of, by host: the host was told to stop nothing but the orphans an operator ended. Any rise means the store may have lost or rolled back its tables.
# TYPE js_unknown_listing_guarded_total counter
js_unknown_listing_guarded_total{host="host-b"} 2
# HELP js_acquires_total Launches the scaler ran, by pool, whatever their answer.
# TYPE js_acquires_total counter
js_acquires_total{pool="gpu"} 3
# HELP js_acquire_failovers_total Launches refused for capacity or quota, after which the scaler tries another offer, by pool.
# TYPE js_acquire_failovers_total counter
js_acquire_failovers_total{pool="gpu"} 1
